@@ -15,3 +15,29 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys and account security
+
+Sign-in supports discoverable passkeys and the existing password service. Sign-up
+creates an account through that service and offers passkey enrollment immediately
+afterward. `/devtools-times/account` provides enrollment, naming, removal, and
+sign-out. Sensitive changes require authentication within the past five minutes;
+the UI prompts for a passkey or password when that period expires.
+
+The same-origin `api/auth/*` routes verify WebAuthn challenges, origins, RP IDs,
+user verification, signatures, and credential counters with SimpleWebAuthn.
+Challenges expire after five minutes and are consumed on verification. Sessions
+use HTTP-only, SameSite cookies and rotate after authentication. Passwords continue
+to be checked by the existing remote service and are not stored locally.
+
+The server requires Node 20 or newer. Passkeys require HTTPS (or localhost).
+Set `AUTH_ORIGIN` to the exact public origin in production, for example
+`https://news.example.com`, especially when using a reverse proxy. Changing the
+hostname changes the relying party and prevents existing passkeys from working.
+
+Credential public keys and sessions persist in `.data/auth.json` by default.
+Set `AUTH_DATA_DIR` to a private persistent volume in deployment. This serialized,
+atomic file store supports one server process; replace `src/lib/auth-store.ts`
+with shared database storage before deploying multiple instances. Do not expose
+this directory as static content. No biometric data or credential private keys
+are sent to or stored by the application.
